From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Oct 2026 11:35:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skippy): restore XIELU unary op params in stage replay

The UNARY replay case recreates activations through ggml_unary, which writes
only the unary op id into op parameters. XIELU is the one unary that carries
extra parameters: ggml_xielu stores four transformed floats (beta +
softplus(alpha_n), softplus(alpha_p), beta, eps) in slots 1-4, and the
extractor already captures them in the program. Replayed XIELU therefore ran
with unset parameters - deterministic zeros from fresh pool memory - so the
staged side computed a different function from layer 0 onward. Apertus, the
only XIELU family, diverged at l_out-0 with ~1.4e3x smaller magnitudes and a
tens-of-nats head gap while every preceding op replayed faithfully.

Restore the first five recorded op-parameter slots verbatim for XIELU.
---
diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
index c134ae58d..65f1fbe50 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program_replay.cpp
@@ -515,6 +515,17 @@ ggml_tensor * replay_operation(
                             static_cast<ggml_unary_op>(operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0)))
                     : ggml_unary(context, sources[0],
                             static_cast<ggml_unary_op>(operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0)));
+            if (tensor != nullptr &&
+                    operation_parameter<int32_t>(operation, 0) ==
+                            static_cast<int32_t>(GGML_UNARY_OP_XIELU)) {
+                // ggml_unary writes only the op id, but ggml_xielu also stores four
+                // transformed activation floats (beta + softplus(alpha_n),
+                // softplus(alpha_p), beta, eps) in op-parameter slots 1-4. Restore
+                // the recorded first five slots verbatim so replayed XIELU matches
+                // the extracted graph; apertus is the only family recording it.
+                ggml_set_op_params(tensor, operation.parameters.data(),
+                        5 * sizeof(int32_t));
+            }
             break;
         case GGML_OP_SSM_SCAN:
             tensor = ggml_ssm_scan(context,
